Given the following code executing under Java 21+, what is the behavior of the Virtual Thread configuration?

Thread.ofVirtual().name(“worker-”, 0).start(() -> {
	System.out.println(Thread.currentThread().isDaemon());
});

Consider the following pattern matching code introduced in recent Java versions:

static void process(Object obj) {
	switch (obj) {
		case String s && s.length() > 5 -> System.out.println(“Long: ” + s);
		case String s -> System.out.println(“Short: ” + s);
		default -> System.out.println(“Other”);
	}
}

What happens if the order of the two String cases is reversed?
